# ESP-IDF Environment

## Environment Variable

```
IDF_PATH = /home/maojianxin/workspace/esp-adf-internal/esp-idf
IDF_VERSION = 5.5.2
```

## Build & Test Commands

When running any build, flash, monitor, or test command, always export the IDF environment first:

```bash
export IDF_PATH=/home/maojianxin/workspace/esp-adf-internal/esp-idf
source $IDF_PATH/export.sh
```

Or inline:

```bash
IDF_PATH=/home/maojianxin/workspace/esp-adf-internal/esp-idf source $IDF_PATH/export.sh && idf.py build
```

## Code Reference

When writing or reviewing **any** C code for this project, the following two locations under
`$IDF_PATH` are the ground truth — always consult them before writing any API call, type, macro,
or CMake dependency.  Do not rely on memory or external documentation alone.

### 1. Component Headers — `$IDF_PATH/components/`

All 109 IDF components live here.  For any IDF API you intend to use:
- Read the corresponding header under `$IDF_PATH/components/<component>/include/` first.
- Verify the exact function signature, parameter types, and return type.
- Check for any `@deprecated` or `@note` annotations that apply to IDF 5.5.2.

Examples of frequently referenced paths (non-exhaustive):

| API area | Header path |
|---|---|
| OTA / app update | `components/app_update/include/esp_ota_ops.h` |
| App description | `components/esp_app_desc/include/esp_app_desc.h` |
| HTTP client | `components/esp_http_client/include/esp_http_client.h` |
| HTTPS OTA | `components/app_update/include/esp_https_ota.h` |
| Flash partitions | `components/esp_partition/include/esp_partition.h` |
| NVS | `components/nvs_flash/include/nvs.h` |
| Wi-Fi | `components/esp_wifi/include/esp_wifi.h` |
| FreeRTOS | `components/freertos/FreeRTOS-Kernel/include/` |
| Error codes | `components/esp_common/include/esp_err.h` |
| IDF version macros | `components/esp_common/include/esp_idf_version.h` |
| System / restart | `components/esp_system/include/esp_system.h` |
| Logging | `components/log/include/esp_log.h` |
| Timer | `components/esp_timer/include/esp_timer.h` |

### 2. Official Examples — `$IDF_PATH/examples/`

The examples are the **canonical usage reference** for every IDF feature.  Before writing new
integration code, check whether a relevant example exists:

```
$IDF_PATH/examples/
  bluetooth/       — BLE / Classic BT examples
  network/         — TCP/IP, MQTT, HTTP, WebSocket
  protocols/       — HTTP server/client, HTTPS OTA, MQTT, Modbus
  storage/         — NVS, FAT, SPIFFS, SD card, wear levelling
  peripherals/     — GPIO, UART, SPI, I2C, ADC, DAC, PWM, ...
  wifi/            — Station, AP, scan, provisioning
  system/          — Heap, task watchdog, deep sleep, console
  security/        — Secure boot, flash encryption, NVS encryption
  lowpower/        — Light sleep, deep sleep power management
  get-started/     — hello_world, blink (baseline reference)
```

Use example code as a reference for:
- Correct initialisation sequences
- Typical configuration struct values
- Error handling patterns
- CMakeLists.txt component dependencies

### 3. IDF Version Policy

- Baseline: **IDF 5.5.2** (`ESP_IDF_VERSION_VAL(5, 5, 2)`).
- Use IDF 5.x APIs and CMake style (`idf_component_register()`).
- Do **not** use deprecated IDF 4.x patterns (`register_component()`,
  `COMPONENT_REQUIRES`, etc.).
- When writing version-gated code (`#if ESP_IDF_VERSION >= ...`), use
  `ESP_IDF_VERSION_VAL(5, 5, 2)` as the known-good baseline.
